// oleg.ae/for-laura: explains to Laura Moiseja (Boldane client) why her 2026-10-14 interviews produced 29 posts.
// Unlisted, noindex. Generated by a one-off script in a Boldane admin session (2026-10-20).
export const HTML = "<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\"><meta name=\"robots\" content=\"noindex, nofollow\"><title>Why you got so many posts</title><meta name=\"description\" content=\"What happened after your interviews on 14 October.\">\n<style>\n:root{--bg:#f6f7f9;--card:#fff;--ink:#14181f;--mut:#5d6573;--line:#e3e6eb;--blue:#2863f0;--green:#15803d;--green-bg:#e8f6ed;--amber:#b45309;--amber-bg:#fdf3e4}\n@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){:root{--bg:#0b0f16;--card:#121823;--ink:#e6e9ee;--mut:#9aa3b2;--line:#242c3a;--blue:#6b93ff;--green:#5bd28a;--green-bg:#122619;--amber:#f0a654;--amber-bg:#2a1f12}}\n*{box-sizing:border-box}html{-webkit-text-size-adjust:100%}\nbody{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font:17px/1.55 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\"Segoe UI\",Inter,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif}\nmain{max-width:680px;margin:0 auto;padding:32px 16px 56px}\nh1{font-size:28px;line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 14px}h2{font-size:20px;margin:36px 0 10px}\np{margin:0 0 12px}.mut{color:var(--mut)}\n.badge{display:inline-block;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;border-radius:999px;padding:3px 10px;margin-bottom:10px}\n.box{border-radius:14px;padding:18px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--card)}\n.new{border-color:var(--green)}.new .badge{background:var(--green-bg);color:var(--green)}\n.old{border-color:var(--amber)}.old .badge{background:var(--amber-bg);color:var(--amber)}\n.post{border-left:3px solid var(--line);padding-left:14px;margin-top:6px}.post p{font-size:16px;margin:0 0 10px}\n.old ul{margin:4px 0 12px;padding-left:20px}.old li{margin:0 0 8px}\n.tip{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:18px;font-size:18px}\n@media (max-width:420px){h1{font-size:24px}}\n</style></head><body><main>\n<p class=\"mut\">For Laura \u00b7 from Oleg</p>\n<h1>Why you got so many posts on 14 October</h1>\n<p>After an interview, the app writes your posts by itself. Since this summer it needs about <b>1 hour</b> to do that. I forgot to tell you. That was my mistake, not yours.</p>\n<p>On 14 October nothing showed up after 30 minutes. So you pressed the <b>\"Generate Content\"</b> button. That button is an older way of writing posts. It added 24 more posts.</p>\n<p>So you got <b>5 good posts + 24 extra posts = 29 posts</b>.</p>\n\n<h2>The 5 good posts (the app made these by itself)</h2>\n<div class=\"box new\"><span class=\"badge\">5 posts, each about a different thing you talked about</span><p>This is what a good post looks like. Here is one of the 5, in full:</p><div class=\"post\"><p>My daughter&#x27;s school has data proving no one can predict what jobs exist in 15 years, but you&#x27;re still hiring for today&#x27;s titles.</p><p>I visited my daughter&#x27;s school recently. She&#x27;s in first grade.</p><p>The employee walking me through it didn&#x27;t mention math levels or exam scores once.</p><p>What she said instead: they have data, based on huge market research, that we can&#x27;t even imagine what kind of positions are gonna be open in the future.</p><p>So the first years are built around how to adapt in new situations, how to be brave, how to talk properly, how to communicate, how to collaborate in different environments with different people.</p><p>Nobody can name the job titles coming. Not the school. Not us. Not the companies hiring right now.</p><p>I&#x27;m also seeing it in the kids. They compare themselves on soft skills now, not grades.</p><p>10-15 years ago none of us thought AI would answer a simple question, or that we&#x27;d have agents replacing assistants.</p><p>Math still matters. Hard subjects still sharpen the brain. But the school building the next generation stopped measuring kids by exam scores a while ago.</p><p>Makes me wonder what you&#x27;re still measuring candidates by.</p></div></div>\n\n<h2>The 24 extra posts (made when you pressed the button)</h2>\n<div class=\"box old\"><span class=\"badge\">24 posts, many telling the same story</span><p>14 of these 24 posts are about the same intern. Here are the first lines of 3 of them:</p><ul><li>An intern scored the lowest possible result on an IQ test I gave her.</li><li>An intern took an IQ test. Lowest possible score.</li><li>A candidate scored the lowest possible result on the IQ test we use for hiring.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:0\">To write so many posts about one story, the old way made up details you never said, like \"founders visibly squirm\".</p></div>\n\n<h2>Next time</h2>\n<div class=\"tip\">Do your interview, then wait about 1 hour. Your posts will be there. Don't press \"Generate Content\". If you still see nothing after 2 hours, message me. The 24 extra posts you can simply delete.</div>\n</main></body></html>";
